stdout:
reference[26]: Set expiry to now + D (positive Go duration). Only an unexpired lease with a,verified live owner on this machine can be extended. It cannot be resurrected.,A --protect-live-owner lease with a live owner also renews after expiry when its,resource is still present (status reattached). Its other refusals exit 3 with,"reason owner_dead, owner_unknown, resource_absent or resource_unknown and leave",the lease unchanged.,"Examples:","  dibs extend <id> --ttl 2h","  dibs extend <id> --ttl 30m --json","",Touch heartbeat files at most every staleness/3. Extend a lease at the latest,when one third of its TTL remains. Owner death OR expiry makes a lease,"reclaimable: a live owner missing either cadence loses its resources.","With --protect-live-owner, only proven owner death reclaims; a late extend",with a live owner reattaches when the resource is still present.,"Output: --axi for agents, --json for scripts (mutually exclusive).","Default: human on terminals; AXI for pipes or DIBS_AXI=1.","Lease commands: --full restores complete AXI records/text; JSON is always complete.","","Exit codes: 0 success (including no-ops), 1 operation failed, 2 invalid usage.","dibs job: child's exit code on completion; 124 deadline killed child;",75 (EX_TEMPFAIL) no slot within wait. Dibs's own 1/2 apply only when no child,was started. Signal termination returns 128 + signal number. Helper/wait,failures after start use 125/126 and diagnostics on stderr.,76 is SSH transport/protocol failure with unknown remote result (stderr).,Child exit 255 is preserved and is not confused with SSH failure.
usage: "dibs extend <id> --ttl D [--json]"
